1
00:00:02,420 --> 00:00:05,787
The temple gardens
are as beautiful as ever.

2
00:00:05,788 --> 00:00:07,470
But being here
always brings back that memory

3
00:00:07,471 --> 00:00:09,037
of the day I was brought here
in critical condition.

4
00:00:10,102 --> 00:00:13,019
Ari saved my life.
She's very important to me.

5
00:00:13,541 --> 00:00:14,919
And yet,

6
00:00:14,920 --> 00:00:17,985
lately, I can't stop
thinking about Miss Restoatt.

7
00:00:19,215 --> 00:00:20,154
Right.

8
00:00:20,155 --> 00:00:24,190
I need to ask people at the temple
what really happened on the day Ari saved me.

9
00:00:24,605 --> 00:00:25,690
Excuse me, miss?

10
00:00:25,691 --> 00:00:27,190
Could you spare me a moment?

11
00:00:27,191 --> 00:00:27,737
Huh?

12
00:00:29,710 --> 00:00:31,331
Mr. Garret!

13
00:00:32,107 --> 00:00:33,761
Sorry to interrupt your work.

14
00:00:33,762 --> 00:00:34,989
When I was gravely wounded,

15
00:00:34,990 --> 00:00:37,395
it was Candidate Saintess Ari
who healed me.

16
00:00:37,396 --> 00:00:38,568
You must have heard about this?

17
00:00:39,543 --> 00:00:40,407
Uh...

18
00:00:42,870 --> 00:00:44,651
About what happened then,

19
00:00:44,652 --> 00:00:47,440
will you tell me everything you know?

20
00:00:49,513 --> 00:00:50,902
What should I do?

21
00:00:50,903 --> 00:00:53,454
Should I confess it to him?

22
00:00:53,455 --> 00:00:56,456
The truth that only I know.

23
00:00:57,393 --> 00:00:59,338
That the one who healed Mr. Garret

24
00:00:59,339 --> 00:01:00,895
wasn't Miss Arianne,

25
00:01:02,733 --> 00:01:04,731
but Miss Lua.

26
00:01:13,630 --> 00:01:16,382
(With Vengeance, Sincerely,
Your Broken Saintess Season 2)

27
00:02:36,610 --> 00:02:38,471
(Episode 8: How to Use an Ability)
What's wrong?

28
00:02:38,472 --> 00:02:40,018
(Episode 8: How to Use an Ability)
If you know something, please tell me.

29
00:02:41,099 --> 00:02:42,921
A-About that...

30
00:02:43,838 --> 00:02:44,868
Commander Garret!

31
00:02:44,869 --> 00:02:46,766
I have an urgent report.

32
00:02:47,313 --> 00:02:48,363
What happened?

33
00:02:48,364 --> 00:02:50,104
Regarding the remaining monsters,

34
00:02:50,105 --> 00:02:53,301
we just got a new report
that someone has been attacked.

35
00:02:54,142 --> 00:02:55,211
Really?

36
00:02:55,691 --> 00:02:58,808
Previous sightings were mostly
on the outskirts of town,

37
00:02:58,809 --> 00:03:00,857
and no one was hurt.

38
00:03:00,858 --> 00:03:02,983
But this time, a man
who happened to be passing by was attacked.

39
00:03:03,542 --> 00:03:06,453
It seems a Candidate Saintess
is treating him as we speak.

40
00:03:07,012 --> 00:03:08,984
But the attack took place

41
00:03:08,985 --> 00:03:11,862
near an old abandoned estate.

42
00:03:13,217 --> 00:03:14,771
An old estate?

43
00:03:14,772 --> 00:03:17,134
The estate of former Baron Restoatt.

44
00:03:17,882 --> 00:03:19,233
Restoatt?

45
00:03:19,719 --> 00:03:21,437
R-Right, I understand.

46
00:03:21,438 --> 00:03:23,147
I'm heading there immediately.

47
00:03:23,487 --> 00:03:26,072
Sorry for stopping you.

48
00:03:27,293 --> 00:03:29,109
This is an emergency,
so I must take my leave.

49
00:03:31,351 --> 00:03:32,512
That's alright.

50
00:03:35,192 --> 00:03:37,536
In the end, I couldn't say it.

51
00:03:38,569 --> 00:03:40,555
Whether it's Miss Arianne's lie,

52
00:03:40,556 --> 00:03:42,822
or the truth about Miss Lua.

53
00:03:43,332 --> 00:03:44,624
Miss Lua.

54
00:03:47,316 --> 00:03:48,395
What's that?

55
00:03:50,004 --> 00:03:51,011
Is that...

56
00:03:52,310 --> 00:03:53,433
A monster?

57
00:03:54,185 --> 00:03:55,400
And just a cub?

58
00:03:55,873 --> 00:03:58,285
There are still monsters undetected
within the kingdom's borders?

59
00:03:58,286 --> 00:04:00,284
I can't just leave it here.

60
00:04:00,285 --> 00:04:01,647
I'll use my torturing ability...

61
00:04:07,432 --> 00:04:09,193
Huh? It didn't hurt...

62
00:04:09,194 --> 00:04:10,458
Louis!

63
00:04:11,908 --> 00:04:13,782
Louis, I'm sorry.

64
00:04:13,783 --> 00:04:14,783
Are you alright?

65
00:04:15,614 --> 00:04:16,981
I'm... I'm fine.

66
00:04:16,982 --> 00:04:19,876
I never thought
a monster would be lurking here.

67
00:04:20,704 --> 00:04:24,512
Louis doesn't know about
my torturing ability yet.

68
00:04:24,513 --> 00:04:27,301
I have to touch that monster
and subdue it quickly.

69
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:31,293
Miss Lua, look out!

70
00:04:33,707 --> 00:04:35,041
Is this poison?

71
00:04:43,472 --> 00:04:44,986
I've inflicted a paralysis effect.

72
00:04:44,987 --> 00:04:46,506
It should be immobile now.

73
00:04:46,507 --> 00:04:47,526
But more importantly...

74
00:04:47,527 --> 00:04:48,489
Louis!

75
00:04:49,040 --> 00:04:50,725
This is likely a deadly poison.

76
00:04:50,726 --> 00:04:52,859
If we wait any longer, he'll die.

77
00:04:53,325 --> 00:04:55,640
Hang in there. I'll heal you right away.

78
00:04:57,201 --> 00:05:00,501
It's been a long time
since I've used my healing ability.

79
00:05:00,502 --> 00:05:02,936
I decided I would never heal anyone again,

80
00:05:03,773 --> 00:05:05,897
but this is no time to hesitate.

81
00:05:06,783 --> 00:05:07,936
Miss Lua.

82
00:05:08,543 --> 00:05:12,784
Please, don't use
your healing ability for me.

83
00:05:13,357 --> 00:05:14,660
What are you saying?

84
00:05:14,661 --> 00:05:15,872
If I don't, you'll...

85
00:05:16,520 --> 00:05:20,014
Your power makes you take on
the other person's suffering.

86
00:05:20,015 --> 00:05:23,317
Yet even so,
you still reach out and heal people.

87
00:05:23,318 --> 00:05:25,688
I've admired that greatly.

88
00:05:26,648 --> 00:05:30,053
But I also made a vow

89
00:05:30,054 --> 00:05:35,082
that I would never rely on that power
and make you suffer in my place.

90
00:05:35,588 --> 00:05:37,571
But still...

91
00:05:37,572 --> 00:05:39,433
Please, don't worry.

92
00:05:39,434 --> 00:05:42,888
I am the son of a merchant
who travels all over the world.

93
00:05:42,889 --> 00:05:44,493
I know a thing or two

94
00:05:44,494 --> 00:05:46,170
about monsters that spit poison.

95
00:05:46,171 --> 00:05:49,249
This venom can be neutralized
by the fruit of the Sabara plant.

96
00:05:50,101 --> 00:05:51,085
What?

97
00:05:51,086 --> 00:05:54,689
But that fruit has a toxic effect
that causes severe stomach pain, doesn't it?

98
00:05:54,690 --> 00:05:58,295
I once treated a person
who accidentally ate one.

99
00:05:58,937 --> 00:06:01,428
That's fighting poison with poison.

100
00:06:02,169 --> 00:06:04,931
As they say,
"Everything can be a medicine."

101
00:06:06,360 --> 00:06:09,869
Because of my family trade,
I'm in the habit of carrying remedies.

102
00:06:09,870 --> 00:06:11,271
I'm sure I put it...

103
00:06:11,878 --> 00:06:12,916
Eh?

104
00:06:12,917 --> 00:06:15,029
I can't find the powdered Sabara fruit.

105
00:06:15,030 --> 00:06:15,861
Did I forget to bring it?

106
00:06:16,952 --> 00:06:18,927
My mind is getting hazy...

107
00:06:18,928 --> 00:06:20,379
H-Hold on!

108
00:06:20,887 --> 00:06:22,413
Wait a minute.

109
00:06:22,414 --> 00:06:26,501
I should be able to use my ability to inflict
the symptoms caused by the Sabara fruit on him.

110
00:06:26,502 --> 00:06:28,533
That way,
without using my healing ability,

111
00:06:28,534 --> 00:06:31,424
I might be able to cure him
by using my torturing ability.

112
00:06:32,582 --> 00:06:33,616
Louis.

113
00:06:33,617 --> 00:06:36,784
I have another ability
I haven't told you about.

114
00:06:37,235 --> 00:06:38,115
Huh?

115
00:06:39,318 --> 00:06:41,968
Thank you for worrying about me.

116
00:06:43,150 --> 00:06:46,372
I trust your knowledge,
so I'm going to treat you now.

117
00:06:50,453 --> 00:06:51,879
This is...

118
00:06:52,505 --> 00:06:54,219
This isn't the healing ability.

119
00:06:54,220 --> 00:06:55,914
It's a power called the torturing ability.

120
00:06:55,915 --> 00:06:58,865
It allows me to inflict the symptoms
I've healed in the past onto others.

121
00:06:59,785 --> 00:07:01,476
I've been keeping this ability a secret,

122
00:07:01,477 --> 00:07:03,489
so keep it a secret for me too, will you?

123
00:07:04,118 --> 00:07:05,636
O-Of course.

124
00:07:06,501 --> 00:07:08,375
Thank you. I'm alright now.

125
00:07:08,376 --> 00:07:09,575
Let's get going.

126
00:07:09,576 --> 00:07:10,430
Yeah.

127
00:07:10,835 --> 00:07:12,209
As for the monster,

128
00:07:12,210 --> 00:07:13,500
I feel a little sorry for it,

129
00:07:13,501 --> 00:07:15,670
but let's leave it paralyzed for now.

130
00:07:16,345 --> 00:07:17,671
You're right.

131
00:07:17,672 --> 00:07:20,883
I'll report this to the knights later.

132
00:07:21,517 --> 00:07:22,789
It really is surprising,

133
00:07:22,790 --> 00:07:26,472
finding another practical use
for the torturing ability.

134
00:07:26,473 --> 00:07:30,016
I'll have to think of other ways
I can use it from now on.

135
00:07:34,130 --> 00:07:35,318
Commander Garret.

136
00:07:35,319 --> 00:07:38,291
It's about the man
who was attacked by the monster.

137
00:07:39,033 --> 00:07:41,895
Right, I recall
getting word at the temple.

138
00:07:41,896 --> 00:07:43,463
What's his condition now?

139
00:07:44,428 --> 00:07:48,015
He lost consciousness for a while
due to the poison spit by the monster.

140
00:07:48,016 --> 00:07:49,639
Fortunately, he eventually came to.

141
00:07:49,640 --> 00:07:52,752
But there's an issue with the man himself.

142
00:07:52,753 --> 00:07:55,231
Apparently, he's actually a wanted thief.

143
00:07:55,232 --> 00:07:56,639
A thief?

144
00:07:56,640 --> 00:07:57,138
Yes.

145
00:07:57,811 --> 00:08:00,876
It seems he was at the abandoned estate

146
00:08:00,877 --> 00:08:03,266
because he had his eye on valuables
inside the property.

147
00:08:03,267 --> 00:08:05,610
But then he was attacked by the monster.

148
00:08:05,611 --> 00:08:06,939
He got exactly what he deserved.

149
00:08:08,003 --> 00:08:11,066
Someone would try
to steal from that estate?

150
00:08:11,067 --> 00:08:13,360
What will she think when she finds out?

151
00:08:14,538 --> 00:08:16,094
Two thieves were reported.

152
00:08:16,095 --> 00:08:17,827
The safety of his accomplice
is still unknown.

153
00:08:17,828 --> 00:08:21,449
He may have also been attacked,

154
00:08:21,450 --> 00:08:23,768
or he could still be lurking on the scene.

155
00:08:24,594 --> 00:08:25,754
Whatever the case may be,

156
00:08:25,755 --> 00:08:27,474
we should hurry to the scene.

157
00:08:33,257 --> 00:08:35,048
My home, after all this time.

158
00:08:36,530 --> 00:08:41,154
The precious place where I lived
with Mother, Father, Lewitt, and everyone else.

159
00:08:42,226 --> 00:08:43,633
Miss Lua,

160
00:08:43,634 --> 00:08:45,980
please watch your step
when we enter the estate.

161
00:08:45,981 --> 00:08:46,706
I will.

162
00:08:51,628 --> 00:08:53,899
It's tidier than I expected.

163
00:08:53,900 --> 00:08:56,388
The state was managing it until recently.

164
00:08:57,235 --> 00:08:59,106
But now that you've gotten the deed back,

165
00:08:59,107 --> 00:09:00,779
I'll help you clean it up.

166
00:09:00,780 --> 00:09:01,826
Thank you.

167
00:09:01,827 --> 00:09:03,406
It will probably be a lot of work.

168
00:09:04,179 --> 00:09:05,011
Hmm?

169
00:09:06,039 --> 00:09:07,504
Footprints?

170
00:09:07,505 --> 00:09:09,116
They're left in the dust.

171
00:09:09,576 --> 00:09:11,901
Has someone been here recently?

172
00:09:11,902 --> 00:09:14,220
Judging by the size,
they must belong to a man.

173
00:09:16,680 --> 00:09:18,147
What was that noise?

174
00:09:18,148 --> 00:09:19,516
Was the window not shut properly...

175
00:09:19,517 --> 00:09:20,726
Shh, stay quiet.

176
00:09:21,364 --> 00:09:22,705
There's someone else here.

177
00:09:22,706 --> 00:09:25,099
Could it be someone
sent by the High Priest?

178
00:09:25,100 --> 00:09:27,308
But the fact that I'm coming here today

179
00:09:27,309 --> 00:09:28,993
should have been kept secret.

180
00:09:29,768 --> 00:09:31,141
Let's check it out.

181
00:09:32,000 --> 00:09:33,507
I'll take the lead.

182
00:09:35,912 --> 00:09:38,111
What happened here?

183
00:09:40,891 --> 00:09:42,148
Don't move.

184
00:09:43,013 --> 00:09:44,097
Miss Lua!

185
00:09:44,785 --> 00:09:47,776
You people are connected to this estate?

186
00:09:47,777 --> 00:09:50,558
Sorry, but I'm taking
everything valuable here.

187
00:09:50,559 --> 00:09:52,068
My partner got attacked by a monster.

188
00:09:52,069 --> 00:09:54,289
Now I'm really backed into a corner.

189
00:09:54,290 --> 00:09:55,670
Just an ordinary thief?

190
00:09:55,671 --> 00:09:58,836
He must have targeted this place
once the state withdrew its management.

191
00:09:58,837 --> 00:10:01,302
It seems this is unrelated
to the High Priest.

192
00:10:01,303 --> 00:10:02,784
But that doesn't mean I'll let you off.

193
00:10:02,785 --> 00:10:05,157
I won't forgive anyone

194
00:10:05,158 --> 00:10:06,940
who tramples on a place I hold so dear.

195
00:10:08,024 --> 00:10:09,787
Not only did you pick the wrong house,

196
00:10:09,788 --> 00:10:12,145
you also picked the wrong hostage.

197
00:10:12,935 --> 00:10:13,702
What?

198
00:10:18,969 --> 00:10:20,042
Wh-What's happening?

199
00:10:26,651 --> 00:10:29,284
I just inflicted the symptoms of hallucinations
caused by a poisonous herb.

200
00:10:29,285 --> 00:10:32,603
It drives a person mad,
making them see their deepest fears.

201
00:10:32,921 --> 00:10:36,088
When I took on those symptoms
to heal someone,

202
00:10:36,089 --> 00:10:38,127
I saw my own family dying.

203
00:10:38,128 --> 00:10:41,408
Inflicting this on someone else
doesn't feel great, either.

204
00:10:42,365 --> 00:10:45,748
Your torturing ability
is truly remarkable, Miss Lua.

205
00:10:46,501 --> 00:10:49,124
I'm sorry I am completely useless.

206
00:10:49,125 --> 00:10:50,610
Don't say that.

207
00:10:50,611 --> 00:10:53,553
Having you by my side
has helped me stay calm.

208
00:10:54,532 --> 00:10:57,793
That thief made this place a mess.
It's harder to find what we need.

209
00:10:57,794 --> 00:11:01,958
Let's start by searching for any clue
that might tell us what my mother wanted to say.

210
00:11:01,959 --> 00:11:02,762
Right.

211
00:11:03,583 --> 00:11:04,669
That being said,

212
00:11:04,670 --> 00:11:07,134
finding a clue won't be easy.

213
00:11:07,135 --> 00:11:08,469
The only hint we have to go on

214
00:11:08,470 --> 00:11:12,049
is the song Mother mentioned,
"Daytime Acclaim."

215
00:11:12,907 --> 00:11:15,075
Could it have something
to do with the piano?

216
00:11:15,076 --> 00:11:16,744
Or does the title itself
hold some meaning?

217
00:11:18,801 --> 00:11:20,346
Wh-What is it?

218
00:11:20,793 --> 00:11:22,222
Sorry to startle you.

219
00:11:22,223 --> 00:11:25,264
I was looking through the bag
the thief was about to take,

220
00:11:25,265 --> 00:11:27,427
and I found a very nostalgic item.

221
00:11:28,653 --> 00:11:29,956
That's what I'm looking for.

